      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal|Guarded Write Journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state (either its previous content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n- If an agent run fails\u2014due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied write attempts\u2014the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n- This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction; the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback functionality since it has no write capability, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
